263
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:18,780
It's the anniversary of the day we met!

264
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:22,120
We're celebrating the day
you became my daughter.

265
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:27,820
Hey, don't cry.

266
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:31,240
It's just a storm so what
if it ruins our crops?

267
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:35,873
You need to learn to be strong girls
who can smile even during hard times.

268
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:39,800
Do that and nothing will ever stop you.

269
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:43,300
Now show me those smiles.

270
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,820
Nami, will you go get the salt?

271
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:50,917
I see you can draw land maps
now as well as sea charts.

272
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,820
I wanted the book to study navigation.

273
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:56,098
Navigation as well?

274
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:58,164
You're going to be a navigator?

275
00:15:58,300 --> 00:15:59,130
That's right.

276
00:15:59,213 --> 00:16:02,057
I'm going to guide ships around
all the oceans of the world.

277
00:16:02,140 --> 00:16:03,022
It'll be great.

278
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,885
And I'll be able to make maps of
all the far-off places I'll go.

279
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:10,637
So, this island map is a first
step toward realizing your dream.

280
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:11,550
Is that it?

281
00:16:11,633 --> 00:16:12,463
Yeah!

282
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:46,580
Well, Bellomere, we finally made it.

283
00:16:47,060 --> 00:16:50,160
It took eight long years,
but we're finally free.

284
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,460
The village and me.

285
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:55,697
It's just like you told
us when we were children.

286
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:59,220
Be brave and smile and nothing
will be able to stop you.

287
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:00,520
It's so true.

288
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:04,780
Arlong's gone and now everybody
is so happy to be free.

289
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:07,980
And me.

290
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,534
I'm finally going to leave this island.

291
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:13,300
But don't worry. I'll be okay.

292
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:16,240
I'm going with good, strong people.

293
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:17,480
Like you.

294
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:21,877
And this last map is
all that I have left to

295
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:24,997
remind me but none of that
really matters anymore?

296
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:28,877
Right because now I'll
start again and every

297
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:31,577
map I draw will be for me and nobody else!

298
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:36,131
Oh you see this time when I see the
world it will be with all of my friends.

299
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:40,173
You know that's what I've always wanted.

300
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:45,717
Anyway I'm just trying to say goodbye.

301
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:47,976
because I don't know if I'll be back.

302
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:58,900
I'm going now, okay?

303
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:26,900
This is the last one, right? Yeah.

304
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,980
Got everything? Yep.

305
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,377
All right, we're stocked
up with everything we need.

306
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:33,931
I think we're good to go.

307
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:37,497
You know, we've only been on this
little island for a few days,

308
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:38,857
but it feels more like a lifetime.

309
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:39,770
Yeah!

310
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:50,457
We can't thank you enough for
everything you've done for us,

311
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:54,011
but we gotta go back to our
regular jobs as bounty hunters.

312
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:55,440
So this is goodbye.

313
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:58,060
I hope we get to meet again someday.

314
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:00,800
See you around.

315
00:19:01,540 --> 00:19:02,370
Goodbye!

316
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:05,440
Yeah, now it's time for us to get going.

317
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:07,740
But we can't leave yet.

318
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:09,277
We gotta wait for Nami.

319
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:11,066
Well, maybe she's not coming.

320
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,020
What? Why not?

321
00:19:13,380 --> 00:19:16,677
If you tried to hit on her again, I
swear I'll break your freaking neck.

322
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:17,590
You got it?

323
00:19:17,673 --> 00:19:18,503
Why would I do something like that?

324
00:19:18,586 --> 00:19:19,977
She might not even be coming.

325
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:21,617
After all, she has achieved her goal.

326
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,757
Nami doesn't have to be a pirate anymore.

327
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:25,477
She might be better off
if she stayed here on

328
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:27,657
this island with all
her friends and family.

329
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:28,977
What about me, damn it?

330
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:30,740
Without Nami on board,

331
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:35,920
I have like 98.72 % less reason to stay
with you people on this stupid pirate ship.

332
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:39,297
Hey, I'm still upset with
you about the raw ham melon.

333
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:41,320
Why is it Nami here? Don't know.

334
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,817
I haven't seen her anywhere
since this morning.

335
00:19:43,900 --> 00:19:44,730
What?

336
00:19:44,813 --> 00:19:46,340
100 million berries?

337
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,320
She left all the money?

338
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:52,840
She's not even gonna take some of
it, but she worked so hard to get it.

339
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:55,060
She'll steal more.

340
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:57,187
That's what her letter said.

341
00:19:57,500 --> 00:20:02,280
Hmm, there's no changing her
mind once it's made up that girl.

342
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:05,440
She didn't even give us
a chance to thank her

343
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,617
I don't get it.

344
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:26,677
Why is she running?

345
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,540
She said to set sail. What?

346
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:34,537
No, she's planning on leaving us without
letting any of us thank her or say goodbye.

347
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:36,200
Hey, wait!

348
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,380
Sit still!

349
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:44,480
Wait! Don't go!

350
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:46,760
They're leaving! Stop!

351
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,647
At least let us say goodbye!

352
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:51,900
Nami, don't!

353
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,300
Let us thank you!

354
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:56,650
Nami!

355
00:20:56,733 --> 00:20:57,563
Come back here!

356
00:20:57,646 --> 00:20:59,091
You can't leave this way!

357
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:01,497
So, you sure you want to
let her leave like this?

358
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:03,140
Not my decision.

359
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:04,920
She does what she wants.

360
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:23,480
Mommy!

361
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:34,710
Why?

362
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:57,077
Huh? No way!

363
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:58,260
Where's my money?

364
00:21:58,380 --> 00:22:00,160
My wallet's gone! Mine, too!

365
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:01,960
She stole my money!

366
00:22:02,100 --> 00:22:03,340
My purse is gone!

367
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:09,640
Thanks a bunch! Damn!

368
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:11,674
Give it a little brat!

369
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,630
Great.

370
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:17,420
She hasn't changed a bit.

371
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:19,460
I'd watch my back.

372
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:26,000
You lousy pickpockets!

373
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:27,360
We'll miss you!

374
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:39,980
Remember what I told you?

375
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:44,157
You got it!

376
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:45,477
Goodbye everybody!

377
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:47,240
I'll miss you. Take care.

378
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:51,600
I can't believe her!

379
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:55,100
My little sister Got us good with that one

380
00:22:56,360 --> 00:22:57,840
Be safe Nami

381
00:23:01,820 --> 00:23:03,377
Take a look at this!

382
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:04,937
What is it, doc?

383
00:23:05,020 --> 00:23:06,097
Nami's bill!

384
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:08,357
Not exactly!

385
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:10,317
That girl will never change.

386
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:11,977
That's her new tattoo!

387
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:13,977
What's it supposed to be?

388
00:23:14,060 --> 00:23:16,440
A tangerine and a pinwheel

389
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,900
Hey, Genzo, where's your pinwheel?

390
00:23:26,260 --> 00:23:28,420
I don't need it anymore.

391
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:41,500
I'm off.

392
00:23:48,820 --> 00:23:50,040
Genzo, back off.

393
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:52,088
Don't get so close to Nami.

394
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:54,280
I just wanted to see her smile.

395
00:23:55,120 --> 00:23:56,840
Your face is too scary.

396
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:58,376
It's making her cry.

397
00:23:59,100 --> 00:24:01,100
I can't change my face.

398
00:24:01,700 --> 00:24:02,530
Oh, wait.

399
00:24:02,700 --> 00:24:05,260
I'll keep this on my hat to distract her.

400
00:24:05,740 --> 00:24:07,564
What do you think, little girl?

401
00:24:08,180 --> 00:24:09,460
You're joking, right?

402
00:24:09,720 --> 00:24:11,337
It's just a stupid pinwheel.

403
00:24:11,420 --> 00:24:13,655
There's no way it's going to make her.

404
00:24:19,340 --> 00:24:21,080
I can't believe it.

405
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:22,140
She's laughing.

406
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:48,837
I'll say goodbye and squeeze your hand.

407
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:51,797
I'll say, say I'm alone, but I'll waste.

408
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:53,797
Now I'm gonna keep you near.

409
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:58,460
As I drift away, I pray you
watch me as I disappear.

410
00:25:04,460 --> 00:25:08,437
As I watch the sunrise, I begin to wonder.

411
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:13,137
What could be the reason
it's so hot inside?

412
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:19,277
No answer has come, but I can't
get away from what's true.

413
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:21,820
It's because of you.

414
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:29,417
Show me how to catch those feelings,
get them to come back to me.

415
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:34,477
I'll do what I must because
they're everything I want will be.

416
00:25:34,560 --> 00:25:39,057
Wrap these arms around my dreams
and pull them back from yesterday.

417
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:44,480
If I'm holding hands with you,
I'm sure that we can make a way.
